  "details": "Currently, if you want a pickup to respond to things like the joystick or jump button, it will happen *alongside* those inputs' normal functions.   This can somewhat be mitigated by changing a player's movement speed to zero, but that will block movement for both hands rather than just the hand holding the pickup;  if we could have something like JavaScript's \"stopPropagation\", we could more accurately replace only certain inputs while a pickup is in use.",
